# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules. The hashed JS/CSS bundles
# already have unique filenames per build (content-addressed), so they're
# safe to cache forever -- but the top-level HTML pages (/, /app,
# /architecture, etc.) share the same URL across deploys, so without an
# explicit rule an edge cache or a visitor's browser can keep serving an
# old build's HTML after a new one ships.
#
# The /* block also carries the site-wide security response headers. No
# Content-Security-Policy yet: three pages still use inline <script>
# (src/content/pages/Community.jsx, src/content/pages/Challenge.jsx, and
# app.html's theme script), so a CSP would need hashes or nonces for those
# first -- deferred, tracked in SECURITY.md's known gaps.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
